From: Simon Jackson <simon@local>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: reinitialize Glymur hosts after power loss

Glymur powers down the DWC3 host state during system suspend. The DWC3
core can already perform a full reinitialization for this case, but the
child xHCI driver is not told that its saved state was lost. It restores
stale DMA ring addresses and faults the SMMU before declaring the host
dead.

Propagate needs_full_reinit to xHCI through its existing power_lost flag,
and select that path for the Glymur single-port and multi-port DWC3
controllers.
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c | 5 +++++
 drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c      | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
index b84e4cc812e7..d4b1ef37c695 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -501,6 +501,11 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	probe_data.res = &res;
 	probe_data.ignore_clocks_and_resets = true;
 	probe_data.properties = DWC3_DEFAULT_PROPERTIES;
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "qcom,glymur-dwc3") ||
+	    of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node,
+				    "qcom,glymur-dwc3-mp"))
+		probe_data.properties.needs_full_reinit = true;
+
 	ret = dwc3_core_probe(&probe_data);
 	if (ret)  {
 		ret = dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to register DWC3 Core\n");
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
index 09a775b9d44d..7dbbd9b103be 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
@@ -110,6 +110,7 @@ int dwc3_host_init(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 {
 	struct property_entry	props[6];
 	struct platform_device	*xhci;
+	struct xhci_plat_priv	priv = dwc3_xhci_plat_quirk;
 	int			ret, irq;
 	int			prop_idx = 0;
 
@@ -168,7 +169,8 @@ int dwc3_host_init(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 		}
 	}
 
-	ret = platform_device_add_data(xhci, &dwc3_xhci_plat_quirk,
+	priv.power_lost = dwc->needs_full_reinit;
+	ret = platform_device_add_data(xhci, &priv,
 				       sizeof(struct xhci_plat_priv));
 	if (ret)
 		goto err;
-- 
